```go
func deleteShadowBranch(ctx context.Context, _ *git.Repository, branchName string) error {
	err := DeleteBranchCLI(ctx, branchName)
	if err != nil {
		// If the branch doesn't exist, treat as idempotent - not an error condition.
		if errors.Is(err, ErrBranchNotFound) {
			return nil
		}
		return err
	}
	return nil
}
```

**Key note:** Shadow branch deletion uses CLI (`DeleteBranchCLI`) instead of go-git's `RemoveReference` because go-git v5 doesn't properly persist deletions with packed refs or worktrees.

#### d) Carry-forward logic (`/Users/gtrrz-victor/wks/cli/cli/cmd/entire/cli/strategy/manual_commit_hooks.go`, lines 2436-2444)

When only partial files are committed, `carryForwardToNewShadowBranch` creates a new shadow branch at the current HEAD with remaining uncommitted files, enabling the next commit to get its own unique checkpoint.

